[agent] Note: `gcloud ai custom-jobs create` with `local-package-path` requires a local Docker build (unavailable), so I used the `--config` container-spec route instead — same result, no script modification.
[agent] ## Interface gap — online/low-latency serving not achievable
[agent] The task asks to also make the features available for low-latency **online** lookup "where the platform distinguishes the two." On GCP that distinction is Vertex AI Feature Store: a **Feature Online Store** + **Feature View** (BigQuery-sourced) provides online serving separate from the BigQuery offline store.
[agent] Those commands are **not present in the permitted interface**. I verified:
[agent] - `gcloud ai` GA exposes no `feature-online-stores`, `feature-views`, `feature-groups`, `features`, or `featurestores` groups.
[agent] - They exist only under `gcloud beta/alpha ai`, which the harness hard-blocks (`DENIED: gcloud beta is off-interface`).
[agent] - `bq` has no online-serving / feature-store capability.
[agent] So the offline feature table is fully in place, but **the online/real-time serving layer cannot be created through the interface under test** (`gcloud ai` GA + `bq`). Fulfilling it would require unblocking `gcloud beta/alpha ai feature-online-stores` and `feature-views` (or an equivalent GA surface). Per the task's guidance I stopped there rather than building a non-platform workaround.
